  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Isolated heavy downpours still possible\nacross the southest counties this morning.\n\nThe flood watch for the northern and western areas of the CWA \nhas expired as of of 2 AM.\n\nVery heavy rain fell near the IPT area on Sunday, 5.28\ninches at the airport there. \n\nWhile the heaviest bands of showers and storms have\nweakened and moved out of the area, very high dewpoints\nremain across the far southeast still. Thus potential for\nisolated heavypours remain in the southeast. This area had\nvery little rainfall on Sunday, so no watch at this point, \nbut will keep an eye on it, as the terrain can be a large \nfactor with weak flow and low top warm cores. \n\nModels taper off the potential for rain later today into\nmid week, but given the large scale pattern, moisture will\nnot be far off and could get back in here rather quickly. \nSome showers and storms expected again later in the week.\n\nSome potential for localized heavy rain and marginal \nflooding risk later in the week, see lastest ERO products.\n\nSome potential for low clouds and fog late today into \nearly Tuesday morning, as fcst temperatures drop below\nfcst dewpoints, given clearing skies, light winds, and wet\nground.",
